00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:30.620
before entering a catalyst-driven name, a step that directly matches recent regime conditions where

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:36.500
rotation has overridden isolated positive developments. The filter keeps positions out of names

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:42.080
already under sector-wide selling pressure, even when company-specific news looks positive at

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:48.540
first glance. The unusual Wales Options Flow Scanner shows large institutional options trades as

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:53.340
they occur, letting investors see whether big players are positioning ahead of earnings or

00:05:53.340 --> 00:06:00.020
sector shifts before the wider market reacts. Canadian users can match the flow data against TSX

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:07.020
names or US holdings inside a TFSA to spot potential early signals. Access begins at the free

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:12.760
tier with paid upgrades available for complete filters and alerts. The platform also supplies

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:18.260
